### 2.2. Cost of Revenue and Gross Margin

While detailed Q2 2023 cost data is pending final audit, the company maintains a strong focus on cost management. Based on the full-year 2024 projections, MedSync Health expects to maintain a high Gross Margin, estimated at approximately 75.0% for the full fiscal year 2024. This is consistent with the high-margin nature of our software-as-a-service (SaaS) business model.

### 2.3. Operating Expenses and Net Income

Operating expenses for Q2 2023 were in line with the strategic plan to invest heavily in Research & Development (R&D) and Sales & Marketing (S&M) to capture market share ahead of the planned Series D funding round (completed in June 2024, post-reporting period).

*   **R&D Investment:** Continued focus on enhancing the MedSync Analytics platform and integrating with major Electronic Health Record (EHR) systems (e.g., Cerner integration completed in April 2023).
*   **Sales & Marketing:** Increased spending on expanding the sales team and launching targeted campaigns in the EMEA region.

